 TRAP←{force}SetTrap G;folder;appName
⍝ General error trapping in case something goes horribly wrong.
⍝ `force` is optional: 1 establishes error trapping, 0 does not, not even in a Runtime, and ¯1, the
⍝ default, establishes it in a Runtime but not in development.
⍝ With 0, HandleError is not asked at all: it would establish error trapping in a Runtime anyway.
⍝ Requires #.ErrorParms to exist!
 force←{0<⎕NC ⍵:⍎⍵ ⋄ ¯1}'force'
 :If ¯1=force
     force←~A.IsDevelopment
 :EndIf
 appName←G.AppName
 folder←⊃G.INI.Get'Trap:Folder'
 #.ErrorParms.errorFolder←folder
 'create!'F.CheckPath #.ErrorParms.errorFolder
 :If 'WIN'≡1 ⎕C ##.APLTreeUtils2.GetOperatingSystem ⍬
     #.ErrorParms.windowsEventSource←appName
 :EndIf
 #.ErrorParms.AppName←appName
 :If force
     TRAP←1 ##.HandleError.SetTrap'#.ErrorParms'
 :Else
     TRAP←⊂(0 1000)'S'                              ⍝ What HandleError returns for "no error trapping"
 :EndIf
⍝Done
